** Agenda

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-c a= | Open agenda dispatcher |
| =C-c c= | Capture (quick entry) |

Agenda files are in =~/Documents/org/=.

** Capture Templates

Press =C-c c= then select a template:

| Key | Template | Description |
|-----|----------|-------------|
| =t= | Todo | Quick task to inbox |
| =n= | Note | Quick note to inbox |
| =h= | Hebrew Note | Note with Hebrew properties |
| =j= | Journal | Daily journal entry |
| =r= | Research | Research note with source |
| =b= | Book | Book to reading list |

** Exporting

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-c C-e= | Open export dispatcher |
| =C-c C-e l l= | Export to LaTeX (.tex) |
| =C-c C-e l p= | Export to PDF via LaTeX |
| =C-c C-e h h= | Export to HTML |
| =C-c C-e o o= | Export to ODT |

*** Export Settings for Hebrew

Add to the top of your Org file:

#+begin_example
,#+TITLE: כותרת המסמך
,#+AUTHOR: שאול
,#+LANGUAGE: he
,#+LATEX_CLASS: article-unlimited
,#+LATEX_HEADER: \\babelprovide[main, import]{hebrew}
,#+OPTIONS: toc:nil
#+end_example

*** Available LaTeX Classes

| Class | Use Case |
|-------|----------|
| =article-unlimited= | Papers, short documents (default) |
| =report-unlimited= | Longer reports with chapters |
| =book-unlimited= | Books with parts and chapters |

All classes support unlimited heading depth and list nesting. Preambles are generated from shared templates to avoid code duplication.

** LaTeX Preview in Org

Preview LaTeX fragments inline:

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-c C-x C-l= | Preview LaTeX fragment at point |
| =C-c C-x C-v= | Toggle inline images |

* Document Systems Overview

This configuration supports three document systems for typesetting:

| System | Best For | Hebrew | Nested Footnotes | Compilation Speed |
|--------|----------|--------|------------------|-------------------|
| *LaTeX* | Academic papers, journals | ✓ (Babel) | Separate blocks (bigfoot) | Slow |
| *ConTeXt* | Complex typography, books | ✓ (native) | Hierarchical (local footnotes) | Medium |
| *Typst* | Fast iteration, modern syntax | ✓ (native) | Sequential | Very fast |

** Quick Document Creation

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-c h n= | Create Hebrew document (choose type) |
| =C-c h l= | Create Hebrew LaTeX document |
| =C-c h x= | Create Hebrew ConTeXt document |
| =C-c h t= | Create Hebrew Typst document |
| =C-c h o= | Create Hebrew Org document |

** Document Systems Hydra (=C-c P=)

#+begin_example
Document Systems

LaTeX:   p: Babel preamble  g: Polyglossia  u: Unlimited struct
         n: Nested footnote template
ConTeXt: c: Hebrew preamble f: Local footnote
Typst:   h: Hebrew preamble s: Nested footnote helper
q: quit
#+end_example

** Comparison: When to Use What

| Scenario | Recommended System |
|----------|-------------------|
| Journal submission | LaTeX |
| Quick draft with live preview | Typst |
| Complex book with local footnotes | ConTeXt |
| Integration with Org-roam | Org → LaTeX export |
| Maximum compilation speed | Typst |
| Maximum typographic control | ConTeXt |

* LaTeX and AUCTeX

** Creating a New Document

1. Create file: =C-x C-f myfile.tex RET=
2. AUCTeX mode activates automatically

Or use: =C-c h l= (or =C-c h n= → =latex=) to create a Hebrew LaTeX document with full preamble.

** Basic Hebrew Document

#+begin_src latex
\\documentclass{article}
\\usepackage{fontspec}
\\usepackage[bidi=basic]{babel}
\\babelprovide[main, import]{hebrew}
\\babelprovide[import]{english}
\\babelfont{rm}{David CLM}

\\begin{document}

\\section{כותרת}

טקסט בעברית.

\\begin{english}
English text here.
\\end{english}

\\end{document}
#+end_src

** AUCTeX Keybindings

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-c C-c= | Run command (compile, view, etc.) |
