* Version Control with Magit

** Keybindings

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-x g= | Magit status |
| =C-x M-g= | Magit dispatch (all commands) |
| =C-c g= | Magit file dispatch |
| =C-c G= | Git timemachine |

** Magit Status Buffer

Press =C-x g= to open the status buffer:

#+begin_example
Head:     main Fix typo in readme
Merge:    origin/main

Untracked files (2)
  new-file.org
  another-file.txt

Unstaged changes (1)
  modified   config.org

Staged changes (1)
  modified   init.el

Recent commits
  abc1234 Fix typo in readme
  def5678 Add new feature
#+end_example

** Basic Workflow

1. Open status: =C-x g=
2. Stage changes: =s= on files (or =S= for all)
3. Commit: =c c=, write message, =C-c C-c=
4. Push: =P p=

** Common Operations

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| =s= | Stage file/hunk |
| =u= | Unstage file/hunk |
| =c c= | Commit |
| =P p= | Push |
| =F p= | Pull |
| =b b= | Switch branch |
| =b c= | Create branch |
| =l l= | Log |
| =d d= | Diff |
| =z z= | Stash |
| =z p= | Pop stash |

** Git Gutter

In programming modes, the gutter shows:
- Green: Added lines
- Red: Deleted lines
- Yellow: Modified lines

** Git Timemachine

Press =C-c G= to browse file history:

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| =p= | Previous version |
| =n= | Next version |
| =g= | Go to specific revision |
| =w= | Copy current version's hash |
| =q= | Quit timemachine |

* Adding New Features

** Adding a New Package

*** Method 1: Edit config.org (Recommended)

1. Open =~/.emacs.d/config.org=: =C-c e i=

2. Find appropriate section or create new heading

3. Add a =use-package= block:

#+begin_example
,** My New Package

,#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package package-name
  :ensure t
  :config
  ;; Configuration here
  (setq some-variable value))
,#+end_src
#+end_example

4. Save the file (auto-tangles to =config.el=)

5. Either:
   - Restart Emacs, OR
   - Place cursor in the block and press =C-c C-c= to evaluate

*** Method 2: Quick Install (Temporary)

1. =M-x package-install RET=
2. Type package name
3. Press =RET=

Note: This won't persist after restart unless added to =config.org=.

** Use-Package Syntax Reference

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package package-name
  :ensure t                      ; Install if not present
  :hook (mode-name . function)   ; Add to mode hook
  :bind ((\"C-c x\" . command))    ; Global keybinding
  :bind (:map mode-map           ; Mode-specific keybinding
         (\"C-c y\" . command))
  :custom                        ; Set custom variables
  (variable-name value)
  :init                          ; Run BEFORE package loads
  (some-setup-function)
  :config                        ; Run AFTER package loads
  (setq some-variable value)
  :after other-package           ; Load after dependency
  :defer t                       ; Lazy load
  :mode \"\\\\.ext\\\\'\"              ; Associate with file extension
  :diminish                      ; Hide from modeline
  :commands (cmd1 cmd2))         ; Autoload these commands
#+end_src

** Common Use-Package Patterns

*** Adding a Hook

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package flycheck
  :hook (prog-mode . flycheck-mode))
#+end_src

*** Adding Keybindings

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package avy
  :bind ((\"M-j\" . avy-goto-char-timer)
         (\"M-g l\" . avy-goto-line)))
#+end_src

*** Loading After Another Package

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package evil-collection
  :after evil
  :config
  (evil-collection-init))
#+end_src

*** Conditional Loading

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package pdf-tools
  :if (display-graphic-p)   ; Only in GUI
  :mode \"\\\\.pdf\\\\'\")
#+end_src

** Adding a New Programming Language

1. Find the major mode package (e.g., =go-mode= for Go)

2. Add to =config.org=:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package go-mode
  :mode \"\\\\.go\\\\'\"
  :hook (go-mode . eglot-ensure)
  :config
  (setq gofmt-command \"goimports\")
  (add-hook 'before-save-hook 'gofmt-before-save nil t))
#+end_src

3. Add LSP server to eglot (if needed):

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'eglot
  (add-to-list 'eglot-server-programs '(go-mode . (\"gopls\"))))
#+end_src

4. For Org Babel support, add:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package ob-go
  :after org
  :config
  (org-babel-do-load-languages
   'org-babel-load-languages
   (append org-babel-load-languages '((go . t)))))
#+end_src

5. Install system dependencies (language, LSP server) via NixOS.

** Adding a New Org Capture Template

In =config.org=, find the capture templates section and add:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'org
  (add-to-list 'org-capture-templates
               '(\"m\" \"Meeting\" entry
                 (file+headline \"~/Documents/org/meetings.org\" \"Meetings\")
                 \"* %^{Meeting Title}\\n  :PROPERTIES:\\n  :DATE: %U\\n  :END:\\n  %?\")))
#+end_src

** Adding a New Org-Roam Template

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'org-roam
  (add-to-list 'org-roam-capture-templates
               '(\"s\" \"sefer\" plain \"%?\"
                 :target (file+head \"%<%Y%m%d%H%M%S>-${slug}.org\"
                                   \"#+title: ${title}\\n#+filetags: sefer hebrew\\n\\n\")
                 :unnarrowed t)))
#+end_src

** Adding a Custom Function

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defun my/custom-function ()
  \"Description of what this function does.\"
  (interactive)  ; Makes it callable via M-x
  ;; Your code here
  (message \"Function executed!\"))

;; Bind to key
(global-set-key (kbd \"C-c x\") 'my/custom-function)
#+end_src

** Adding a New Hydra Menu

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defhydra my/hydra-example (:color blue :hint nil)
  \"
My Custom Menu

_a_: Action A    _b_: Action B
_c_: Action C    _q_: quit
\"
  (\"a\" some-function-a)
  (\"b\" some-function-b)
  (\"c\" some-function-c)
  (\"q\" nil))

(global-set-key (kbd \"C-c X\") 'my/hydra-example/body)
#+end_src

** Adding a New Snippet

1. Create snippet directory:

#+begin_src shell
mkdir -p ~/.emacs.d/snippets/MODENAME-mode/
#+end_src

2. Create snippet file (e.g., =~/.emacs.d/snippets/org-mode/hebrew-header=):

#+begin_example
# -*- mode: snippet -*-
# name: Hebrew Document Header
# key: hebhead
# --
#+TITLE: ${1:כותרת}
#+AUTHOR: שאול
#+DATE: `(format-time-string \"%Y-%m-%d\")`
#+LATEX_CLASS: article-unlimited

$0
#+end_example

3. Reload snippets: =M-x yas-reload-all=

4. Use: Type =hebhead= and press =TAB=

** Reloading Configuration

| Keybinding | Action |
|------------|--------|
| =C-c e i= | Open config file |
| =C-c e r= | Reload config |

Or manually:
1. Delete =~/.emacs.d/config.el=
2. Restart Emacs

* All Hydra Menus

** Direction Controls (=C-c D=)

#+begin_example
Direction Controls

r: RTL (Hebrew)    l: LTR (English)    t: Toggle direction
h: Hebrew spell    e: English spell    b: Both languages
B: Toggle bidi     w: Focus writing    W: Set width
q: quit
#+end_example

** Org-Roam (=C-c R=)

#+begin_example
Org-Roam

f: Find node       i: Insert node      c: Capture
l: Toggle buffer   g: Graph            t: Add tag
d: Daily today     D: Daily date       u: Roam UI
q: quit
#+end_example

** Document Systems (=C-c P=)

#+begin_example
Document Systems

LaTeX:   p: Babel preamble  g: Polyglossia  u: Unlimited struct
         n: Nested footnote template
ConTeXt: c: Hebrew preamble f: Local footnote
Typst:   h: Hebrew preamble s: Nested footnote helper
q: quit
#+end_example

** LaTeX Footnotes (=C-c F=)

#+begin_example
LaTeX Footnotes (Simple)

1: \\footnote    2: \\footnoteB   3: \\footnoteC   4: \\footnoteD   5: \\footnoteE
6: \\footnoteF   7: \\footnoteG   8: \\footnoteH   9: \\footnoteI   0: \\footnoteJ

n: Nested template   m: → Marks menu   t: → Texts menu
q: quit
#+end_example

*** Footnote Marks Sub-menu

#+begin_example
Footnote Marks (for nesting)

2: \\footnotemarkB   3: \\footnotemarkC   4: \\footnotemarkD   5: \\footnotemarkE
b: ← Back   q: quit
#+end_example

*** Footnote Texts Sub-menu

#+begin_example
Footnote Texts (for nesting)

2: \\footnotetextB   3: \\footnotetextC   4: \\footnotetextD   5: \\footnotetextE
b: ← Back   q: quit
#+end_example

** Seforim Library (=C-c S=)

#+begin_example
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 📚 SEFORIM                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ FIND FILE          │ SEARCH TEXT                   │
│  f find (indexed)  │  s search all (indexed)       │
│  F find (fuzzy)    │  r search all (ripgrep)       │
│                    │  c search current dir         │
│                    │  S search choose dir          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ NAVIGATE           │ MANAGE                        │
│  o outline         │  I reindex all                │
│  t toggle sidebar  │  ? status                     │
│  b browse root     │                               │
│  B browse current  │                               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     q quit
#+end_example

* Troubleshooting

** Startup Issues

*** Packages Not Installing

#+begin_example
M-x package-refresh-contents RET
#+end_example

Then restart Emacs.

*** Slow Startup

First startup is slow due to package installation. If still slow:

1. Check =*Messages*= buffer for errors
2. Run: =emacs --debug-init=
3. Profile: =M-x profiler-start RET RET= ... =M-x profiler-report=

*** Config Changes Not Taking Effect

After editing =config.org=:

1. Delete =~/.emacs.d/config.el=
2. Restart Emacs

Or manually tangle: =M-x org-babel-tangle RET=

** Hebrew and RTL Issues

*** Hebrew Not Displaying

1. Check fonts installed:
   #+begin_src shell
   fc-list | grep -i \"david\\|nachlieli\\|miriam\"
   #+end_src

2. Check input method:
   : C-h v current-input-method RET

3. Check direction:
   : C-h v bidi-paragraph-direction RET

*** Hebrew Footnotes Showing as LTR in Org

Use =C-c h f= to fix all existing footnotes. New footnotes are fixed automatically.

*** Bidi Performance Issues

For very large files, disable bidi: =C-c B=

** Spell Checking Issues

*** Spell Check Not Working

1. Check hunspell:
   #+begin_src shell
   which hunspell
   hunspell -D
   #+end_src

2. Verify =en_US= and =he_IL= dictionaries are listed

3. Check DICPATH:
   #+begin_src shell
   echo $DICPATH
   #+end_src

4. Switch to correct language: =C-c s e= or =C-c s h=

*** Word Incorrectly Flagged

Press =i= when correcting to add to personal dictionary (=~/.hunspell_personal=).

** Document Compilation Issues

*** LaTeX Compilation Fails

1. Check =*TeX Help*= buffer for errors
2. Ensure LuaLaTeX installed:
   #+begin_src shell
   which lualatex
   #+end_src
3. View log: =C-c C-l=

*** ConTeXt Compilation Fails

1. Ensure ConTeXt installed:
   #+begin_src shell
   which context
   #+end_src
2. Check font access:
   #+begin_src shell
   echo $OSFONTDIR
   #+end_src

*** Typst Compilation Fails

1. Ensure Typst installed:
   #+begin_src shell
   which typst
   #+end_src
2. Check error output in compilation buffer

*** Typst LSP Not Working

1. Ensure tinymist installed:
   #+begin_src shell
   which tinymist
   #+end_src
2. Start eglot manually: =M-x eglot=

** PDF Issues

*** PDF Not Opening in Emacs

Run once:
: M-x pdf-tools-install RET

*** PDF Renders Incorrectly

Ensure =poppler= is installed on your system.

** Org-Roam Issues

*** Database Errors

: M-x org-roam-db-sync RET

*** Nodes Not Appearing

1. Check file has =#+title:= property
2. Ensure file is in =~/Documents/roam/=
3. Rebuild database: =M-x org-roam-db-sync=

** Seforim Library Issues

*** \"Command not found\" Errors

Ensure tools are installed via NixOS and in =$PATH=. Restart Emacs after installing.

*** Slow Search

1. Build indexes: =C-c S I=
2. Use indexed search (=C-c S f=, =C-c S s=) instead of fallbacks

*** No Search Results for Hebrew

Check files are UTF-8 encoded:
#+begin_src shell
file -i yourfile.org
#+end_src

Convert if needed:
#+begin_src shell
iconv -f ISO-8859-8 -t UTF-8 oldfile.org > newfile.org
#+end_src

** Getting More Help

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| =C-h r= | Emacs manual |
| =C-h k= | Describe keybinding |
| =C-h f= | Describe function |
| =C-h v= | Describe variable |
| =C-h m= | Describe current mode |

After pressing a prefix key, wait for which-key popup.

